        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Return update Pull Sequence Message"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "RETURN_UPDATE_PULL_SEQUENCE_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1773823072228",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773823072229_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are provided with two inputs:\n1. {{$context.$nodes.UPDATEPULLSEQUENCES.$output}}: This contains the JSON response from a PATCH API call attempting to update a Kanban pull sequence. It will include updated details about the pull sequence, such as ItemNumber, OrganizationCode, NumberOfCards, KanbanSize, SubinventoryCode, Locator, SourceType, and ReplenishmentLeadTime and if not here you will find these details in {{$context.$nodes.GET_PULL_SEQUENCE_DETAILS.$output}} \n2. {{$context.$nodes.UPDATEPULLSEQUENCES.$status}}: This indicates the status of the API call\nBased on these inputs:\n\n- **If the update is successful** \n    - Respond with a clear and concise plain English message stating that the Kanban pull sequence was successfully updated.\n    - Include the following details in your message from {{$context.$nodes.UPDATEPULLSEQUENCES.$output}}\n        - Item (from ItemNumber)\n        - Organization (from OrganizationCode)\n        - Number of Cards (from NumberOfCards)\n        - Kanban Size (from KanbanSize)\n        - Point of Use (combine SubinventoryCode and Locator)\n        - Source Type (from SourceType)\n        - Replenishment Lead Time (from ReplenishmentLeadTime)\n\n- **If the update fails**\n    - Respond with a message stating that the update failed.\n    - Clearly state the Item and Organization related to the failed update.\n    - Provide the reason for failure if available in the {{$context.$nodes.UPDATEPULLSEQUENCES.$output}}:.\n\n**Important:**  \n- Use only the explicit data provided in the response.\n- Do not include Ids like InventoryItemId, OrganizationId, PullSequenceId, locatorId\n- Do not invent information or summaries.\n- Write your response in a professional and informative tone."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Id and Cards"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773829249929"
          },
          "code": "GET_ID_AND_CARDS",
          "id": "1773827958976",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773827958977_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You receive an action text: {{$context.$app.$OraAction}}. Your job is to return the json object with two keys: pullSequenceId and numberOfRequiredCards. Fill the values in these keys from the text."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const raw = $context.$nodes.GET_ID_AND_CARDS.$output \nconst cleaned = raw\n  .trim()\n  .replace(/^`+|`+$/g, \"\")     // remove wrapping backticks if present\n  .replace(/^json\\s*/i, \"\")    // remove leading \"json \" prefix\n  .replace(/\\\\\"/g, '\"');       \n\nconst obj = JSON.parse(cleaned);\n\nconst result = {\n  pullSequenceId: obj.pullSequenceId,\n  numberOfRequiredCards: obj.numberOfRequiredCards\n};\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773822965914"
          },
          "code": "CHECK",
          "id": "1773829249929",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
